900 C1$="David spoke.":C2$="Andrew spoke.":C3$="Martin spoke.":C4$="Alan spoke.":C5$="Susanna spoke."
2100 GOSUB 6160:BM$="And so, Eleno Vision was ready to begin their last concert in Europe.":GOSUB 5100
2110 BM$="The band was giving it their best during the performance, and once again\the audience was reaching the peak of their excitement.":GOSUB 5100
2120 GOSUB 6100:BM$="Halfway through the song, David called out to the audience, who shouted\back in response.":GOSUB 5100
2130 '
2140 '
2150 GOSUB 6200:BM$="Even though David was speaking in English to a German crowd, it seemed as\if there was no language barrier between them.":GOSUB 5100
2160 BM$="David: We're all allies! We're all in the same clan!":GOSUB 5100
2170 BM$="Audience: YEAH! We're allies!":GOSUB 5100
2180 GOSUB 6150:BM$="The entire audience stood up. Between the German language and the\furious atmosphere, the situation was starting to feel like a scene out of\a Nazi rally.":GOSUB 5100
2190 GOSUB 6120:BM$="David: Kill the traitor!":GOSUB 5100
2200 GOSUB 6200:BM$="Audience: YEAH! Kill the traitor!":GOSUB 5100
2210 GOSUB 6120:BM$="David: Sever the blood of the betrayer!":GOSUB 5100
2220 GOSUB 6150:BM$="Audience: Kill! Kill! Kill! ......":GOSUB 5100
2230 GOSUB 6260:BM$="The eyes of the audience were bloodshot. They were screaming as if their\throats were being crushed.":GOSUB 5100
2240 GOSUB 6120:BM$="David: The traitor is finally dead!":GOSUB 5100
2250 GOSUB 6230:BM$="As soon as David's proclamation ended, Alan pressed his hands on the\keyboard. The audience let out a yell, and the performance began anew.":GOSUB 5100:'
2260 GOSUB 6210:BM$="On the stage, David seemed to grow larger. Though the audience was\reaching the peak of their excitement, there were no disturbances.":GOSUB 5100
2270 GOSUB 6150:BM$="A number of women fainted, but they were carried away by the staff\without incident.":GOSUB 5100
2280 GOSUB 6250:BM$="While Martin was playing his guitar solo, David approached Andrew.":GOSUB 5100
2290 GOSUB 6300:BM$="David: Let's skip the ballad. The crowd's excited but it's all under control. I\say we keep the ball rolling and call it a success.":GOSUB 5100
2300 GOSUB 6330:BM$="Andrew: That's so weird! They're so excited, but they're all moving in\rhythm! Well, sounds good to me. Let's see how far we can go!":GOSUB 5100
2310 GOSUB 6320:BM$="Alan: What are you doing, guys? I'm waiting for yo - Huh? We're skipping the\ballad? Fine by me. Come on!":GOSUB 5100
2320 ISET X:GOSUB 6130:BM$="Martin also seemed to understand. He plucked the strings of his guitar\rhythmically, waiting for the song to start. David shouted to the crowd.":GOSUB 5100
2330 GOSUB 6100:BM$="David: This is the end of our tour of Europe. I'm going to keep singing until I\drop!":GOSUB 5100
2340 GOSUB 6200:BM$="Audience: YEAH!":GOSUB 5100
2350 GOSUB 6240:GOSUB 9525:BM$="The band kept playing, in a frenzy. By the end of it, David could barely let\his voice out. The audience was so excited they were literally ripping\their shirts off.":GOSUB 5100
2360 ISET X:COMMON FO:GOSUB 6160:BM$="Then, as he promised, David finally collapsed on the stage.":GOSUB 5100
2370 BM$="There was not a single person in the venue who had the energy to stand.\Even the members of the staff were leaning against the wall. They were all\in a daze, beyond the point of satisfaction.":GOSUB 5100
2380 BM$="Though the concert was over, the staff did not even have the energy to\turn off the lights or lower the curtains. David, Alan, Andrew, and Martin\themselves were in a daze, on top of the stage.":GOSUB 5100
