2500 GOSUB 6330:BM$="Andrew: You okay, David?":GOSUB 5100:RETURN
2510 GOSUB 6300:BM$="David: Yeah. I can barely move, but I've never felt better.":GOSUB 5100:RETURN
2520 GOSUB 6330:BM$="Andrew: I've never felt like this before. I think I'm going to cry.":GOSUB 5100:RETURN
2530 GOSUB 6300:BM$="David: Andrew, why didn't the crowd go wild this time?":GOSUB 5100:RETURN
2540 GOSUB 6330:BM$="Andrew: Don't ask me. I can't even think right now. Let's just say it all went\well and leave it at that.":GOSUB 5100:RETURN
2550 GOSUB 6320:BM$="Alan: David, what was that thing about a traitor, and the blood of the\betrayer?":GOSUB 5100:RETURN
2560 GOSUB 6300:BM$="David: Huh? Did I actually say that?":GOSUB 5100:RETURN
2570 GOSUB 6310:BM$="Martin: Now that you mention it, I started feeling this sense of unity after\you said that weird stuff.":GOSUB 5100
2580 GOSUB 6175:GOSUB 5821:LINE (0,0)-(500,65),0,BF:BM$="Right then, the lights were turned off, and the curtains were closing.":GOSUB 5100
2590 BM$="There was a round of applause as the curtains fell; however, the audience\had no more energy left, so it felt like the quiet end to a classical concert.":GOSUB 5100
2600 BM$="Susanna: Way to go, David! I'm glad it's over, honestly. My knees are\trembling so much I can barely walk.":GOSUB 5100
2610 BM$="Though the spotlights focused on the band as they walked out, there was\no commotion. After a brief interview, they got into their cars and left\the venue.":GOSUB 5100
2620 GOSUB 6180:BM$="Back at the hotel, David and the others headed back for their rooms, not\having the energy to celebrate.":GOSUB 5100
2630 COMMON FO:BM$="David fell asleep the moment he crawled into his bed, without even having\the time to think.":GOSUB 5100
2640 GOSUB 9515:GOSUB 6110:BM$="The next day, the airport was filled with Union Jack flags, which were\waved until Eleno Vision's plane was no longer visible.":GOSUB 5100
